gold_thread:
Regarding using middleware, you can access the function's arguments (and therefore the logger) with the `transformInput()` hook, e.g.:
```ts
export const logMiddleware = new InngestMiddleware({
  init() {
    return {
      onFunctionRun() {
        return {
          transformInput({ ctx }) {
            // `ctx.logger` is the logger
          },
        };
      },
    };
  },
  name: "Logger ALS Middleware",
});
```
I'd probably then use the `afterExecution()` hook (as it looks like you're doing) to remove it from your async hooks store.

The likely cause of some confusion is that the `logger` is, internally, also middleware, so the types for it aren't shown in userland middleware. 🙄 There's an old PR inngest/inngest-js#332 that resolves this. I'll look at pulling that in to make this path a bit more obvious in the future.

